{"rule": "Return this JSON object with the rule field unchanged and a new passage of about 250 words in the text field.", "text": "The lighthouse keeper climbed the spiral staircase every evening at dusk, counting the one hundred and twelve iron steps as his father had taught him. At the top, he wiped salt from the great glass lens with a soft cloth, checked the oil, and wound the clockwork that turned the beam across the water. The island was small enough to walk around in an hour. It was bare except for wind-bent grass, a stone-walled vegetable garden, and a shed full of tools older than he was. Supply boats came twice a month, bringing flour, letters, and newspapers already a week out of date. The coast guard had written more than once to say the light would soon be automated, that a machine could do his work without sleep or complaint. He had read the letters carefully and filed them in a drawer. On clear nights he could see the lights of the fishing fleet strung along the horizon like beads, and he imagined the men aboard glancing up at his beam and knowing where the rocks lay. In a leather logbook he recorded the weather, the passing ships, and anything else worth remembering: the gannets nesting on the western cliff, the winter a seal pup slept for three days on the landing, the storm that shattered two panes and left him bailing water until dawn. When morning came and the beam faded into gray light, he put out the lamp, brewed strong tea, and sat by the window watching the sea, lonely perhaps, but certain he was needed."}
